<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('partials/head') %></head>
<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">56 isolated vulnerable labs · L1-L6 progression</div>
    <h1>Break real vulnerabilities.<br><span class="gradient-text">Learn how to stop them.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">ZeroDay Academy is a hands-on web security range by <strong>ZeroDay Security Services</strong>. Every challenge is a deliberately vulnerable application with a per-user, per-instance flag — exploit the target, capture the flag, and study the fix after you solve it.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <% if (currentUser) { %>
        <a href="/challenges" class="btn btn-primary">Enter the lab range</a>
        <a href="/dashboard" class="btn btn-ghost">View dashboard</a>
      <% } else { %>
        <a href="/register" class="btn btn-primary">Create free account</a>
        <a href="/challenges" class="btn btn-ghost">Explore labs</a>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="glass stat"><div class="num"><%= stats.challengeCount %></div><div class="label">Vulnerability labs</div></div>
      <div class="glass stat"><div class="num"><%= stats.domainCount %></div><div class="label">Attack domains</div></div>
      <div class="glass stat"><div class="num"><%= stats.userCount %></div><div class="label">Active operators</div></div>
      <div class="glass stat"><div class="num"><%= stats.solveCount %></div><div class="label">Flags captured</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="level-strip">
      <% (levelCounts || []).forEach(row => { %>
        <div class="level-pill">
          <span class="level-tag level-<%= row._id %>">L<%= row._id %></span>
          <span><%= row.count %> labs</span>
        </div>
      <% }) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="margin-top:1rem;">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h2>From brief to flag to fix</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="challenge-grid">
    <div class="glass panel">
      <div class="step-number">01</div>
      <h3>Read the brief</h3>
      <p>Each lab includes a scenario, objectives, OWASP/CWE references and progressive hints. Prerequisites keep the L1-L6 path coherent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass panel">
      <div class="step-number">02</div>
      <h3>Attack the live target</h3>
      <p>The target is a real, isolated Express application with its own per-instance data. Flags are derived server-side and never shipped in page source.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="glass panel">
      <div class="step-number">03</div>
      <h3>Submit and study the writeup</h3>
      <p>Submit the flag from the platform workspace. Points, domain progress, achievements and a post-completion solution unlock automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="glass panel" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
      <h3>Mapped to the work</h3>
      <span class="badge badge-owasp">OWASP Top 10</span>
    </div>
    <p>Every lab is tagged with OWASP Top 10 / API Top 10, ASVS, WSTG, CWE and MITRE ATT&amp;CK references. The same corpus is visible in the lab explorer and admin catalogue.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
